summary:
  Paying the owed flush leaves the debt on the book.

history:
  Measured 2026-09-20 on a JBL Flip 7, five builds out of five (a boot and
  four panel restarts): a group built while nothing plays, its Bluetooth
  transport bounced 1.2 s later by the birth flush, was a dead pipe once the
  music started — sink RUNNING, loopback at 100 %, transport active, nothing
  in the air. With the bounce removed from the installed copy: three builds,
  three live speakers, no backlog. Under flowing music the same bounce was
  harmless four times, and it is what woke the dead pipe every time.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
          _birthFlushOwed = ({});
          app.exec(": PW_FLUSH; " + cmd + "true # " + app.nextSeq());

replace:
          _birthFlushOwed = _birthFlushOwed;
          app.exec(": PW_FLUSH; " + cmd + "true # " + app.nextSeq());

expect:
  Killed by tst_syncengine::test_the_owed_flush_is_paid_once_when_sound_flows.
  Line-neutral.
